{"availability":"available","full":"thakurabhishek7283/tessera-realtime","name":"tessera-realtime","description":"Presence, chat, WebRTC video calls and comment threads as framework-agnostic Web Components. Runs across tabs with no backend.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-02-08T08:30:07Z","updated":"2026-10-05T13:04:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://thakurabhishek7283.github.io/tessera-realtime/","topics":["chat","typescript","web-components","webrtc"],"demo":"https://thakurabhishek7283.github.io/tessera-realtime/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.252Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.252Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.252Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.252Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pluggable realtime for any web app: presence, chat, WebRTC video calls and comment threads. Part of the Tessera kit family: switch a feature on with configuration, use it in any framework, run it across browser tabs with no backend or against tessera-server.","Chat, calls and comments are in almost every collaborative product, and each one tends to arrive with its own backend, its own socket handling and its own framework glue. These kits sit on the small Tessera core instead: they talk through a transport and a storage adapter, so the same code runs between two tabs of one browser (which is how the live demo works, with nothing to host), against the reference server, or against your own backend. A feature you do not enable never loads its code, and every UI piece is a web component, so it works in React, Angular, Vue or plain HTML."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thakurabhishek7283/tessera-realtime/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ad7a04e0e68b42a4ca649aba45aa4834fdeaef50a4774267a46a7a6243415374","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.357Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"